{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"5680efcad1144c071e529054da459b25f4d19d478b914805a8ba24c4f189e369","packTokens":3618,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":627,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":742,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1928,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Replace the current manual processes with a single platform covering stock, orders, deliveries, live temperature monitoring, quality decisions and recalls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a responsive web portal for warehouse staff, dispatchers, quality staff, administrators and auditors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a customer portal for hospitals, pharmacies and clinics.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a driver experience that keeps working without a connection.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Receive temperature readings from data loggers and cold-room sensors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep a centralized shared record of stock, orders and temperature history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Support secure sign-in, role and warehouse access controls, customer-organization isolation, and read-only auditor access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Define versioned product temperature profiles and stability budgets.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Receive stock by lot, track inbound logger readings, quarantine stock, and release it through quality review.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Let customer users place, view, change and cancel orders under the specified delivery and order rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Allocate released stock to orders by earliest expiry while respecting shelf-life, availability and order-completion rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Pack stock into qualified shipper boxes and plan routes with drivers and vehicles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-13\",\n  \"text\": \"Store and process delayed, duplicated and out-of-order temperature readings reliably.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-14\",\n  \"text\": \"Detect excursions, charge stability budgets, place affected stock on hold, and alert relevant users.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-15\",\n  \"text\": \"Enable drivers to load, drive and record delivery handovers using their phone, including offline use.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-16\",\n  \"text\": \"Support the portals in English and Arabic, with Arabic displayed right to left.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-17\",\n  \"text\": \"Track recalled lots, block remaining stock and account for customer responses.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What must the full two-person quality decision for stock exposed to a not-permitted temperature range require?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Quality Officer proposes the disposition and a different Quality Manager approves it; neither person can perform both steps.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When an excursion opens, how quickly must affected stock be placed On Hold relative to the alert deadline?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Place it On Hold as soon as the excursion is detected; the two-minute deadline applies to alerts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"What customer evidence must the driver record for a delivery handover?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record the recipient's name and an explicit electronic acknowledgment of receipt; a drawn signature is not required.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen to quantities that are not handed over because a delivery is refused or only partly completed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep undelivered quantities outstanding; record the reason and return them to available stock only after warehouse receipt and any required quality checks.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What constitutes a handling unit for tracking stability budgets when a received quantity is split, moved, or packed into different boxes?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Track quantities as handling units and split the record whenever portions acquire different temperature histories.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may maintain a customer organisation's saved delivery addresses and minimum remaining shelf-life requirement?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Customer Administrators maintain their organisation's addresses; System Administrators set its minimum shelf life.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the stock quantity breakdown reconcile with quantity on hand, given that stock can also be On Hold, Rejected, Recalled or Expired?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat on-hand as the total and show a mutually exclusive breakdown that includes available, allocated, quarantined and the other stock statuses.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When a product profile changes with an effective date, how should the new profile affect stock already received and its temperature-budget history?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the new version to stock still held from its effective date onward and recalculate affected budgets and decisions from that date.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build Meridian as a responsive web app with role-oriented portals and navigation for stock, orders, deliveries, temperature monitoring, quality decisions, and recalls across phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide staff sign-in through Meridian Microsoft accounts; customer email-and-password sign-in followed by a one-time code; and customer password-reset requests by email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Show records and actions returned for each user's role, assigned warehouses, and customer organisation; make Auditor views read-only; and clear protected data when access is refused.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Let Customer Administrators invite and remove users within their organisation, and maintain that organisation's saved delivery addresses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Let System Administrators list, search, view, deactivate, and maintain products; set organisation-level minimum remaining shelf life; and create versioned temperature profiles with storage bands, contiguous non-overlapping tiers, allowance or not-permitted designations, a reason, and an effective date, while keeping earlier versions read-only.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Show API-returned recalculated budgets, decisions, current workflow statuses, notices, and errors for stock affected by an effective-dated profile change, including affected stock already released, allocated, packed, or delivered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Let Warehouse Operators record receipts with product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and storage location, upload inbound logger files and separate image or PDF receipt evidence, and view returned quarantine status, temperature history, readings, and budget use before release.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Present quality staff with available receipt-release and excursion-disposition actions and API-returned decision states, including separate proposal and approval steps for not-permitted-range dispositions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Show on-hand stock and mutually exclusive quantities for available, allocated, quarantined, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired statuses, together with returned warehouse, lot, product, receipt, and location details; show handling units separately when their temperature histories differ.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Provide stock-movement forms and show returned movement records with source and destination locations, quantity, actor, and time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Let customer users create orders with one or more product lines, pack quantities, an organisation-saved delivery address, an eligible delivery date, and a choice between delivery of available quantities and complete delivery only; show the organisation's minimum remaining shelf-life value read-only on customer and Dispatcher order forms.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Show order status and allocated and outstanding quantities per line; expose customer change and cancellation controls only before Packed and Dispatcher cancellation controls when returned as available; and display returned API outcomes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Show order allocations by line and lot, including expiry dates and quantities; provide Dispatcher lot-override controls with a required reason; and show returned allocation and stock-status outcomes in order, box, and route views.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Let Warehouse Operators pack stock into shipper boxes by type, associate one logger with each box, and show returned compatibility, contents, quantities, sealing, operator, and time details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Let Dispatchers create and view routes with a date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times; and show API-returned confirmation errors, configured qualified-duration safety margins, confirmed-route changes, schedule details, and driver notification status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Show temperature histories for boxes, cold rooms, and lots as charts and tables with returned readings, applicable bands, excursions, gaps, flags, and silence status; display returned histories in time order without presenting excluded readings as calculation inputs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Show returned excursions, handling-unit budget use and remaining allowances, alerts, hold statuses, and quality decision statuses for affected devices and stock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Show unresolved temperature-history gaps, review status, and returned On Hold stock status without estimating a temperature tier or charging an unobserved tier, until the gap is resolved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Show API-returned quality-review cases to relevant customer and staff users when corrected temperature history identifies an excursion affecting stock already delivered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an installable, responsive driver web experience that caches the current workday's assigned route and queues supported loading and delivery actions offline for synchronization when connectivity returns; show stale-route, queued-action, synchronization, and refusal outcomes returned by the API.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Let drivers record delivery handovers with recipient name, explicit electronic acknowledgment, quantities handed over, and any refusal or partial-delivery reason; show outstanding quantities and returned delivery status without requiring a drawn signature.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Show returned warehouse receipts and quality-check results for undelivered stock returned to a warehouse, and show the stock as available only when the API reports it available.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Let Quality Managers view and manage recalls, including returned lot locations, affected deliveries, quantities, and blocked remaining stock; let customer users submit a quantity and stated disposition for each affected delivery; and show returned reconciliation and outstanding quantities without requiring supporting-document upload.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Provide filtered on-screen operational lists and CSV export, and show creator and last-changer identities and timestamps as read-only metadata where returned.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Provide English and Arabic portal content, rendering Arabic pages right to left and English pages left to right.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Ensure every portal page reflows for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow layouts; conform main staff, customer, and driver web flows to WCAG 2.1 Level AA; support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox; and support the stated first-year user and record volume and simultaneous device volume.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}